selec 1 -> invalid sql: near "selec": syntax error
select 1; select 2 -> invalid sql: One statement per `sql(...)`: split it into one call per statement.
select :a -> invalid sql: Parameters are `?`, taken from the list in order; named and numbered parameters are a second spelling.
select random() -> invalid sql: `random()` reads randomness: compute the value in vo (std.random) and pass it as a parameter.
select datetime('now') -> invalid sql: `'now'` reads the clock: compute the time in vo (std.time) and pass it as a parameter.
pragma journal_mode = wal -> invalid sql: PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL is not available in vo
select * from no_such_table -> run: no such table: no_such_table
select ? + 1 -> 1 row(s)
